+## Rejections that are not Error instances
+
+- A rejection that is not an `Error` instance — a thrown string, plain object, or `undefined` — calls `onError` once with an `Error` whose `cause` is the original rejection; the original value is re-thrown to the caller unchanged ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with a string, and re-throws the original string](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- The same wrapping holds when the rejection is a plain object ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with a plain object, and re-throws the original object](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+- And when the rejection is `undefined` ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with undefined, and re-throws undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
 This property of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` is recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue does not change it; that is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
